# --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Wave 2 additions. The corpus carried eight expected discrepancies across fourteen cases, one
# per kind, no case with two at once and no boundary anywhere. A 0.90 recall bar tolerates one
# miss only over ten scored positives, so the bar was arithmetically identical to 1.0 while
# reading as though it had headroom; and one-discrepancy-per-case is not what a presentation
# looks like, so nothing measured whether the detector finds the SECOND problem once it has
# found the first.
#
# Three shapes are added, each of which the corpus could not previously express:
#
#   multi-*      two, three and four simultaneous discrepancies. A detector that stops at the
#                first finding scores full marks on the old corpus and fails here.
#   near-miss-*  the Article 14 hard case, on both sides of the configured description overlap
#                floor: wording that differs and means the same thing must be ACCEPTED, wording
#                that differs enough must be refused. A corpus with only obvious mismatches
#                pins neither side of that line.
#   art30-*      the amount and latest-shipment boundaries at the configured policy: exactly at
#                the credit and one cent over; on the last shipment day and one day after. A
#                boundary nobody tested is a boundary that moves in a refactor.
#
# All parties, credits and goods are fictional.
